; BUILT WITH `-checked` -- `go run ./cmd/build -checked …`.
;
; `(go.+ (go.at-map m w) 1)` cannot be bounded: nothing declares what a
; `map[string]int` holds, and a range on the PRIMITIVE would be a claim about
; every use of it rather than about this program. The language's own map
; carries a value range in its type and would fix it -- `(map string (int 0
; 65535))` -- but string keys wait on strings.md. So this takes ADR 0019's
; second escape: the trap instead of the proof.
;
; Gauntlet program 4 — word frequency — on the NATIVE Go target.
;
; The portable form is examples/wordcount.oro, and its pass condition was never
; a number: the Go output must use Go's own map[string]int, and the JS output a
; null-prototype object. On the portable layer that took `dict-empty`,
; `dict-inc` and `split-words` — three names whose whole job was to hide which
; host construct was chosen.
;
; Here there is nothing to hide. `go.make-map` IS `make(map[string]int)`,
; `go.at-map` is `m[k]`, and `strings.Fields` is Go's own splitting. The
; Parasite thesis is not being tested by the reducer any more; it is just true
; by construction, and what the migration tested instead was whether the target
; could SAY it — the native Go target had no string surface at all until this
; program asked for one.
;
; Note what `dict-inc` becomes: `m[w] = m[w] + 1`. Go's map read returns the
; zero value for an absent key, so no presence test is needed.
;
; TWO FORMS, which is the rule for adding to the gauntlet — and the first draft
; of this file asserted the answer instead of carrying both. It reasoned that
; reaching for the host's clever API would be slower, because the baseline
; measured Java's fused `merge` LOSING 2.6x to unfused getOrDefault+put. That
; reasoning is right about Java and WRONG about Go, where `m[w]++` is one
; mapassign against a mapaccess plus a mapassign, and wins by 1.21x. Exactly the
; rule it violated: never assert which host construct is fastest (ADR 0008).

(use go)
(use go/strings)

(export tally tally-inc)

(sig tally     ((text string)) map-string-int)
(sig tally-inc ((text string)) map-string-int)

(def bump     (fn (m w) (go.set-map m w (go.+ (go.at-map m w) 1))))
(def bump-inc (fn (m w) (go.inc-map m w)))

(def count-with (fn (step text)
  (let (strings.Fields text) (fn (ws)
    (loop ((m (go.make-map)) (i 0))
      (go.>= i (go.len ws))  m
      else                   (again (step m (go.at-string ws i)) (go.+ i 1)))))))

(def tally     (fn (text) (count-with bump     text)))
(def tally-inc (fn (text) (count-with bump-inc text)))
